<!--
    kuna GH-851: a caller that reads only the high word of a callee's 64-bit
    result printed it as a local nothing assigns, next to a bare call.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 call output prototype (FuncCallSpecs::
    buildOutputFromTrials, p4_calls/kuna_callretpair.rs build_partial_pair).
    P0 assertion: option callretpair off|on (on is the shipped default).

    hib is `bl full; uxtb r0,r1`: r0 is overwritten unread, so only the r1
    output trial is active, and no output rule returns r1 without r0. The
    call kept no output and r1 rendered as an unassigned local. With the fix
    the call returns the r1:r0 pair the model joins, and r1 is a SUBPIECE of
    it. hiplus (`add r0,r1,#7`) and hiw (`mov r0,r1`) are the same shape.

    The Thumb functions at 0x1100 are the Cortex-M forms: hibt reads r1
    through `uxtb r0,r1`, and lo40t reads r0 and the byte r1:1 (`uxtb r1,r1;
    eor r0,r0,#1`), which left the pair five bytes wide and r1:1 unassigned.

    Controls: lob reads only r0 and prints the same in both passes. hig32
    reads r1 after calling g32, whose decoded body never writes r1 (a value
    gcc -fipa-ra could keep there across the call), so its call keeps no
    output in both passes. hip reads r1 after an indirect call: there is no
    callee body to show a write (a MIPS PIC call to a static function is
    indirect too, and gcc keeps values in $v1 across it), so it also keeps
    its bare call.

    Source of the bytes (clang -target armv7a / thumbv7m assembler):
        full:  add r1,r0,#1; add r0,r0,r0,lsl #1; bx lr
        g32:   rsb r0,r0,r0,lsl #3; sub r0,r0,#100; bx lr
        hib:   push {r11,lr}; bl full; uxtb r0,r1;        pop {r11,pc}
        hiplus:push {r11,lr}; bl full; add r0,r1,#7;      pop {r11,pc}
        hiw:   push {r11,lr}; bl full; mov r0,r1;         pop {r11,pc}
        lo40:  push {r11,lr}; bl full; uxtb r1,r1; eor r0,r0,#1; pop {r11,pc}
        lob:   push {r11,lr}; bl full; add r0,r0,#1;      pop {r11,pc}
        hig32: push {r11,lr}; bl g32;  add r0,r1,#7;      pop {r11,pc}
        hip:   push {r11,lr}; blx r0;   mov r0,r1;         pop {r11,pc}
        fullt: adds r1,r0,#1; add.w r0,r0,r0,lsl #1; bx lr          (Thumb)
        lo40t: push {r7,lr}; bl fullt; uxtb r1,r1; eor r0,r0,#1; pop {r7,pc}
        hibt:  push {r7,lr}; bl fullt; uxtb r0,r1; pop {r7,pc}

    Pass 1 (off) pins the bug: bare calls and unassigned r1 locals. Pass 2
    (on) pins the pair output and its SUBPIECEs. The controls do not move.
-->
